  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"All marginalia in Walden Marginalia were rendered in the artist's hand, conformed to the dimension of the first edition of Walden, and printed from photopolymer plates on a Vandercook No. 3.  The text was hand-set in Scotch roman and Bodoni types, the closest approximation of those used in the first edition.  The paper is Zerkall Book Vellum.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This artist's book examines margin notes found in 12 copies of Walden, while providing commentary on the reading habits of strangers, assumptions about nature writing and learning, and the lingering effects of Thoreau's classic work. By withholding the original text to focus solely on these marks, Walden Marginalia turns the same kind of close attention Thoreau inspired in his readers onto the readers themselves."--Women's Studio Workshop website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 50 copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes "Bibliography of Waldens."</subfield>
  </datafield>
